{
  "description": "#3830 — the READ differential over the three KEYED COUNT commands, the last group whose waivers all read 'returns a keyed count map, not the canonical block-id rows the query projection binds'. `count_trash` answered that for a BARE scalar (`count_trash#value=<n>`); the generalisation is one token per map entry, `<key>#count=<n>`, with the nested `date -> source -> count` map spelled `<date>-><source>#count=<n>` (`count_map_tokens` / `countMapTokens`). The seed exists to make the counts DISCRIMINATE: three delete cohorts of different depths for `trash_descendant_counts` (one of them a root whose only child was tombstoned by an earlier op, so it has no descendant in its OWN cohort), and four dated blocks for `count_agenda_batch_by_source`, one of them due and scheduled on the same day so the `(date, block_id)` precedence rule is visible. The dates arrive through OPS rather than the seed because `agenda_cache` is materialized: `set_due_date` / `set_scheduled_date` enqueue `RebuildAgendaCache`, a seed insert would not. `count_backlinks_batch`, the third command of the group, is driven by `query_backlinks.json` instead — that fixture's link set already discriminates.",
