      "command": "trash_descendant_counts",
      "comment": "Four roots asked about, two answered. S2 counts TWO (S3 and S4, tombstoned by its cascade in the same `deleted_at` cohort) and S7 counts ONE (S8) — different counts, so a mock that answers the same number for every key differs on one of them. S5 is ABSENT: its only child S6 was deleted by an EARLIER op, so S6 sits in a different cohort and the recursive CTE's `c.deleted_at = d.batch_deleted_at` join refuses to follow the edge; the `count > 0` guard then drops the key entirely rather than reporting 0. S1 is absent for a second, independent reason — it is LIVE, and `rb.deleted_at IS NOT NULL` never seeds the walk from it, so a mock that walks a live root's subtree counting tombstones answers seven here.",
      "name": "trash_descendant_cohort_counts"
    },
    {
      "args": {
        "dates": ["2026-07-01", "2026-07-02", "2026-07-03"],
        "scope": {
          "kind": "active",
          "space_id": "$SPACE"
        }
      },
      "command": "count_agenda_batch_by_source",
      "comment": "The nested map, one token per (date, source). 2026-07-01 holds TWO `column:due_date` rows (S9, S10) and ONE `column:scheduled_date` (S11) — differing counts under one key. 2026-07-02 holds ONE: S12 is both due and scheduled that day, and `agenda_cache`'s PK is `(date, block_id)`, so `DESIRED_AGENDA_SQL`'s priority order keeps the higher-precedence `column:due_date` row and drops the scheduled one — a mock that counts the two columns independently answers a second source here. 2026-07-03 is absent: a date with no rows is omitted, not carried as an empty map.",
      "name": "agenda_counts_by_date_and_source"
    },
    {
      "args": {
        "dates": ["2026-07-01", "2026-07-02"],
        "scope": {
          "kind": "global"
        }
      },
      "command": "count_agenda_batch_by_source",
      "comment": "The harness has one space, so `Global` (`?2 IS NULL`) selects the same rows and the counts are unchanged. What it pins is that this command SERVES `Global` unscoped rather than refusing it the way `count_trash` does.",
      "name": "agenda_counts_global_scope"
    },
    {
      "args": {
        "dates": ["2026-7-1"],
        "scope": {
          "kind": "active",
          "space_id": "$SPACE"
        }
      },
      "command": "count_agenda_batch_by_source",
      "comment": "`count_agenda_batch_by_source_inner` validates every date before it queries (`validate_date_format`), and chrono's `%Y-%m-%d` would otherwise accept the unpadded form. Only the SHAPE is pinned here: a calendar-invalid but well-shaped date (2026-02-30) is refused by chrono on the backend, which the mock's regex mirror does not model.",
      "expect_error": "validation",
      "name": "agenda_rejects_malformed_date"
    }
